{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534539-for-fun-hollow-one-to-deviant","id":1534539,"title":"For Fun - Hollow One to Deviant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-21T21:06:55-07:00","id":1534539,"title":"For Fun - Hollow One to Deviant","content":"Cross-splat hypothetical: you are a Mage, and have managed to &quot;cure&quot; a Hollow One! ...by turning them into a Deviant. What did you do, and what does the Deviant looks like? (i.e. Scars, Variations, Clade, Origin)<br /> <br /> Amnesia 5 seems like a given, for example, and any level of Frozen Heart could be thematic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-22T08:01:12-07:00","id":1534555,"title":"","content":"(...)<br /> Attempt 1: We couldn't access the victim's Oneiros, so our plan to implant a replacement Daimon couldn't continue as intended. It's possible that at present the Hollow One does not possess an Oneiros in the first place, therefore next time we'll attempt to patch the injured pattern from the outside. It's for the best, too - after the failed attempt, my apprentice refuses any futher Astral jaunts. Since she experienced 60 hours-worth of sensory deprivation during the minute she was inside, I don't blame her.<br /> <br /> Attempt 2: Upon being sent into the injury, the Daimon slowly melted and &quot;spaghettified&quot; into the patient, screaming agonizingly throughout the process. All attempts to resummon it from the patient failed. Divinations suggest this caused no long-term improvement to the patient's wellbeing. I'm writing this having rewound time an hour, so the Daimon is still safe. Its donor may still be under arrest, but he is still deserving of future self-improvement.<br /> <br /> Attempt 3: Having the Daimon possess the Hollow One did not have the intended effect. The patient snuck out of our Sanctum and was caught accosting the donor outside his cell, beseeching him to mend his ways and take up crocheting for some reason. Clearly, the Daimon is still connected to its original owner, so we must redirect his link inwards. My Goeticist associates say there is precedent for that.<br /> <br /> Attempt 4: Success! At least a partial one. The patient showed signs of volition and curiousity, but is still dependent on Seer &quot;programming&quot;. After his last personality timed out and was restarted, all mental and emotional progress was reset, which is a bummer. On the other hand, his memories of begging me to recharge his batteries to prolong his &quot;life&quot; are gone too, so I might have dodged a bullet here.<br /> <br /> Attempt 5: Progress! We managed to enhance the Daimon with a human-level mind, so it can preserve the patient's memories and experiences across multiple resets. For as long as Mana lasts, our setup adequately compensates for Hollow One's soul damage, restoring the patient to being a complete person - just with a mind floating outside of his head like a baloon. Speaking of souls, I also outfitted the Daimon with a database of soul lore. This will be necessary for an upcoming attempt. My Hedge-practitioner subordinates provided me with a high-school swimming trophy that they say if filled with soul-stuff. Mind-aspected soul-stuff, if I understand correctly, naturally resublimated. The Daimon's combined awareness of patient's metaphysical state and it's new soul-expertise should be enough to let it complete the repairs.<br /> <br /> Attempt 6: I f***** up! I shouldn't have let the Daimon work on its own. I don't know what it did, but now the patient remembers everything! He was really upset about about Attempts 2 and 4, so I rewound time before today's procedure. It didn't work! He remembered the lost hour and got even angrier. I tried to detach the Daimon, but it's stuck fast, and it got the patient really pissed. I didn't know he knew Krav Maga... wher did he even learn that!? I hid in the cellar until he stormed out of the Sanctum. The chief Jailor is going to kill me.<br /> (...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}